  "turns": [
    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well, Dr. Smith... I guess I'm here because of work. The warehouse. It's... the routing system there, it isn't just a regular computer to me anymore. I've been operating the trucks there for a long time, you know? Back when I started, we just used paper manifests. My old manager, Gary, he used to keep everything on this battered yellow legal pad. Gary was a real character—he actually won a few thousand on a scratch-off ticket once and bought a used Corvette. Bright red. Always parked it way in the back so nobody would ding the doors. \n\nBut, uh, what was I saying? Right, the new system. I know it's been marking my moves. Every time I beep a barcode, it's sending these messages through the scanners, communicating, trying to push me out because I'm one of the old hands. They want the older guys gone. Which reminds me, I need to take my own truck in for an oil change soon, the check engine light came on Tuesday when I was pulling into the employee lot, and I just haven't had the time to get under the hood...",
