    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "You mentioned the scanner is communicating with you; do you actually hear voices coming from the scanner, or is it more of a feeling that it is sending you messages?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "It's... it's actual voices, Dr. Smith. It's not just a feeling. It started at the warehouse, but now... now it doesn't even matter where I am. Even when I'm just sitting out in my garage, you know, with the doors pulled down and the engine shut off, I hear them. Clear as day. It's the dispatch voices. They call out my operator number over and over, saying I'm dangerous, saying security is coming to get me. \n\nMy garage used to be my quiet place, you know? I've got this old workbench in there that belonged to my father-in-law. Solid oak. He built it himself back in the seventies before he lost his sight. He was a carpenter, a real craftsman. Made these beautiful birdhouses, too—intricate little things with shingles and everything. We had one hanging in the oak tree out back for years until a storm knocked it down in '08. That was a bad storm, took down power lines all over the county. We were eating canned beans over a camp stove for three days. My wife—God rest her soul—she made a game out of it, pretending we were pioneers... \n\nBut anyway, yeah. The voices. They just keep calling my number, telling me they're coming for me, even when I'm just sitting there at that oak workbench in the dead quiet.",
