    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "How long have you been hearing these voices from the dispatchers?",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "Well, let's see... it's been a while now. I'd say the voices and, you know, all this stuff with the scanners and them trying to push me out, it's been going on for about a year and eight months. Almost two years. It started right around the time they brought in those new electric pallet jacks. \n\nMan, those things are quiet. Too quiet, if you ask me. You used to be able to hear a forklift coming from three aisles over, you know? The hum of the propane, the clanking. Now, these young kids zip around corners on those electric ones, not even honking the horn. Almost took my toes off twice in one week. And they wear those ear pods while they drive! We'd have been fired on the spot back in Gary's day for having headphones on the floor. Gary was strict about safety. He used to make us watch these terrible safety videos from the eighties, the ones where the actors would dramatically fall off a loading dock in slow motion. We'd always laugh, but he meant well. \n\nBut yeah, anyway, the dispatch voices... it's been about a year and eight months since they started calling my number.",
