    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Aside from hearing these voices, have you noticed any other changes in how you think, like difficulty organizing your thoughts, or have you found it harder to take care of your daily routines, like grooming or eating, since this started?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S022",
      "patient_response": "Well, it's funny you ask about getting mixed up, because lately, yeah, I do get real turned around. At work, and even sometimes when I'm just at home, I get so mixed up that I'll just stand there holding my hands out in front of me, like they're still on the forklift controls, you know? And I'll be repeating this same safety phrase over and over, out loud, while folks are just standing there trying to talk to me. \n\nIt's like I'm stuck on a loop. Speaking of loops, I used to collect these old reel-to-reel tapes. Had a whole setup in the basement. I found this one tape at a garage sale out in Springfield—guy wanted two bucks for it, but I talked him down to a dollar. Turns out it was an old radio broadcast from 1964, a local baseball game. The announcer had this incredible voice, real deep and smooth. I used to listen to it on Sundays while I was polishing my boots. I always bought Red Wing boots. They cost a pretty penny, but if you take care of the leather, they'll last you a decade. You gotta use the mink oil, though, not that cheap silicone spray. The silicone dries out the stitching... \n\nBut anyway, yeah, I just stand there holding my hands like I'm driving the lift, saying the safety words over and over. It's like my brain just stalls out.",
